  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Norec, FK Norway, personnell exchange</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malawi, Zambia, Zimbabwe. Sports and recreation opportunities for children and youth are unfortunately not widespread or even prioritized in many countries of the world. In particular, there are considerable inequalities to access according to age and gender. This is the case in Africa as well, where the project aims to operate. Sports and recreation are considered an important part of child development, providing skills and behavioural frameworks that can accompany a person over its lifetime. In addition, participating in sports alleviates stress and impacts positively in mental health, including of course children. Even though Norway stands out as country with good enabling conditions for children in sports, there is nonetheless, room for improvement and the project has identified specific challenges for including women and young girls in sports.  

The project aims to create Safe, inclusive and sustainable sports environments for children and youth in all the partner countries. They expect to do this by:

1-	Engaging children and youth in sports activities
2-	Increase competence and opportunities for young coaches; and
3-	Capacity building for the implementing agencies</narrative>
  </description>
